<title>GERMANY: German joblessness to cost 180 bln DM in 97 -report.</title>
<headline>German joblessness to cost 180 bln DM in 97 -report.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's record unemployment will cost the country around 180 billion marks this year, a newspaper reported on Friday.</p>
<p>Citing unpublished data from the Federal Labour Office's research arm, the mass daily Bild newspaper said each person on the government dole cost 41,000 marks a year but that the recipient of jobless benefit received only 12,095 marks.</p>
<p>The lion's share of the costs for unemployed went towards covering insurance, social security payments and tax shortfalls, the report said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097 150</p>
</text>
